---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { software, drone } from "../data/site";
import { getPosts, formatDate } from "../lib/content";

const droneThumbs = import.meta.glob<{ default: ImageMetadata }>(
  "../assets/drone/*.jpg",
  { eager: true },
);

const recent = (await getPosts()).slice(0, 3);
---

<Base sidebar>
  <h1>About me</h1>

  <p class="lede">
    I am a Research Software Engineer and the Founder of{" "}
    <a href="https://catalystneuro.com">CatalystNeuro</a>, where I work on the data
    standards and software infrastructure that let neuroscience labs share their data
    and build on each other's work.
  </p>

  <h2>Vision and Work</h2>

  <p>
    Neuroscience produces an enormous amount of data, but very little of it is in a
    form that another lab can pick up and use. At CatalystNeuro we work on the
    practical side of that problem: developing standardized formats for
    neurophysiology data, building conversion and analysis tools that labs can
    actually adopt, connecting analysis platforms that would otherwise stay siloed,
    and working directly with labs to reshape their data workflows. Much of this
    happens through <a href="https://nwb.org">Neurodata Without Borders</a> and the{" "}
    <a href="https://dandiarchive.org">DANDI Archive</a>, alongside a large community
    of contributors.
  </p>

  <p>
    The through line is that standardization is worth doing only if the tools around
    it are good enough that using them is easier than not using them. That is where
    most of my attention goes.
  </p>

  <h2>Software</h2>

  <p>
    Side projects, the things I build outside of work. The neuroscience software is
    CatalystNeuro's and lives at{" "}
    <a href="https://catalystneuro.com">catalystneuro.com</a>.
  </p>

  <ul class="software">
    {
      software.map((s) => (
        <li>
          <div class="software__head">
            <a href={s.href}>{s.name}</a>
            <span class="software__tag">{s.lang}</span>
            {s.stars && (
              <span class="software__stars">
                <span aria-hidden="true">★ {s.stars}</span>
                <span class="visually-hidden">{s.stars} stars on GitHub</span>
              </span>
            )}
          </div>
          <p>{s.blurb}</p>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ul>
  <p><a href="/software/">All software</a></p>

  <h2>Recent Writing</h2>

  <ul class="entries">
    {
      recent.map((post) => (
        <li>
          <a class="entry__title" href={post.data.permalink}>
            {post.data.title}
          </a>
          <div class="entry__meta">{formatDate(post.data.date)}</div>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ul>
  <p><a href="/posts/">All posts</a></p>

  <h2>Background</h2>

  <p>
    I received my Ph.D. in Bioengineering from the{" "}
    <a href="https://bioegrad.berkeley.edu/">
      UC Berkeley - UCSF Joint Program in Bioengineering</a
    >, working in <a href="https://changlab.ucsf.edu/">Dr. Edward Chang's lab</a>. My
    research used electrocorticography (ECoG) to study speech motor control in humans,
    particularly the neural mechanisms of voice pitch control in speaking and singing.
  </p>

  <p>
    As an undergraduate at the University of Pittsburgh, I worked in the{" "}
    <a href="https://smile.pitt.edu/">SMILE lab</a> with{" "}
    <a href="https://www.engineering.pitt.edu/AaronBatista/">Dr. Aaron Batista</a> on
    probabilistic models of neural activity. That early work shaped how I think about
    neural data analysis, and it is a fairly direct line from there to my interest in
    standardizing data practices across the field.
  </p>

  <h2>Alternative Paths in Science</h2>

  <p>
    I am interested in non-traditional careers in science, and CatalystNeuro is one
    example of what those can look like. I work with a team of neuroscientists and
    software developers who came to this work from a range of backgrounds, most of
    them not the standard academic track.
  </p>

  <p>
    If you are considering a path like this, or just want to hear how it has gone,
    feel free to reach out at{" "}
    <a href="mailto:ben.dichter@catalystneuro.com">ben.dichter@catalystneuro.com</a>. I
    am happy to talk about it.
  </p>

  <h2>Outside Work</h2>

  <p>
    I dance West Coast Swing and travel as much as I can manage. Those two overlap
    more than you would expect, and one of them turned into a project:{" "}
    <a href="https://westie.wiki">westie.wiki</a>, a community wiki for West Coast
    Swing moves.
  </p>

  <p>
    I fly a drone when I travel. A few of the results are on{" "}
    <a href="https://www.youtube.com/@bendichter4116">my YouTube channel</a>:
  </p>

  <ul class="reel">
    {
      drone.map((clip) => {
        const thumb = droneThumbs[`../assets/drone/${clip.id}.jpg`]?.default;
        return (
          <li>
            <a href={`https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=${clip.id}`}>
              <span class="reel__thumb">
                {thumb && (
                  <Image
                    src={thumb}
                    alt=""
                    widths={[240, 480]}
                    sizes="(max-width: 30rem) 45vw, 14rem"
                    loading="lazy"
                  />
                )}
                <span class="talk__play" aria-hidden="true" />
              </span>
              <span class="reel__place">{clip.place}</span>
              <span class="reel__where">{clip.where}</span>
            </a>
          </li>
        );
      })
    }
  </ul>
</Base>
